-- [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast
    ["80331"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast",
    ["Description"]="Whoa, whoa, easy there, champ! I can see you're chomping at the bit to tame a wild beast, but there's a catch. Us goblins don't exactly get along with nature, know what I mean?<Viz grins wryly.>Let me show you how it's done, the goblin way. See this rod? It comes with a special collar that I call the \"Friend Request\". You put this around any wild animal's neck and that beastie becomes your bestie, get me?Probably oughta start you on something easy. A Dire Mottled Boar should be simple. You'll find them wandering around just outside of Razor Hill.Even a kid like you should be able to do that much. So don't waste my time by coming back here without one!",
    ["Objectives"]="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Dire Mottled Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Viz Fizbeast in Razor Hill.",
    ["Progress"]="Go on, then. Show ‘em who's boss.",
    ["Completion"]="So you're not completely incompetent. Alright then, let's really test your beast-wranglin' skills!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast

-- [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast
    ["80332"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast",
    ["Description"]="You see kid, every time you add a pet to your collection you become stronger. Your pet is like an extension of you. We goblins may not be the strongest, but we got the biggest brains. Let the animal be your strength while you make with the plans!That goes double for showing 'em who's boss, feel me? Why wrestle a beast into submission when you can outsmart 'em?Let's turn things up a notch. You're gonna have to get your boots wet for this next critter. This one really likes the sea, particularly past that Troll village down south.You know the one... Sen'jin Village? Down near the Echo Isles. Keep your eyes peeled for a Surf Crawler, slap the ol' \"Friend Request\" on 'em, and bring it back to me.",
    ["Objectives"]="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Surf Crawler. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Viz Fizbeast in Razor Hill.",
    ["Progress"]="Well? C'mon, kid! If you can't even tame a crab, you can kiss your dreams of taming a crocolisk goodbye!",
    ["Completion"]="You made that look easy! You got a bright future in this hunter business, pal. You'll be bagging dragons in no time.You can take that to the bank. I got a good intuition about these sorta things.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast

-- [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast
    ["80333"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast",
    ["Description"]="Time for your final exam, champ. You better be ready, 'cause otherwise you ain't coming back breathing. Our Orc friends call these babies Armored Scorpids.They're quick on their tiny legs, and their carapace is light yet durable. Kinda goes with the whole \"armored\" thing. They got a deadly sting to boot, so if you get your hands on one, ain't no one gonna push you around no more, ever.When you get back, I'm gonna show you something real nice. Let me tell you, pal, these skills are beyond mad! You'll be able to tame whatever beast you want, and call 'em and dismiss 'em at your leisure.",
    ["Objectives"]="Use the Taming Rod to tame an Armored Scorpid. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Viz Fizbeast in Razor Hill.",
    ["Progress"]="Move it, kid. You want to miss your chance to be a legendary beast-tamer? I mean, same goes for dying to scorpid venom, so... Don't take that big a chance.",
    ["Completion"]="Look at you, kid! You grew up so fast. It's enough to make this old goblin tear up. Almost. Thanks for the merchandise. These are some great specimens. Now, you're gonna have to choose one of your own.I've taught you all I know and given you my spare collar. It's pretty much unbreakable, but try to be careful with it anyway, alright?You can summon and dismiss a pet whenever you want from now on. Flex that confidence you been building up with this training and all the critters in the land will call you master before long.In no time at all, you and your pet will make an unstoppable duo! Payment due for these lessons when that day comes, by the way.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast

-- [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast
    ["80334"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast",
    ["Description"]="One last tip, kid! For a small addition to your tab, of course. There's an orc in Orgrimmar who goes by the name Ormak Grimshot. He can teach you how to train the beasts you tame.What? You thought you were gonna become a big-shot hunter with a pet who can't learn some fancy tricks? I like you, kid: you're a laugh!You can find Ormak in the Valley of Honor, as the orcs call it. Now hit the road! Next time we meet, it'll be when I'm on your doorstep to collect my payment.",
    ["Objectives"]="Speak with Ormak Grimshot in Orgrimmar.",
    ["Progress"]="",
    ["Completion"]="A young YOUR_CLASS, I see. Yes, I will grant you the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.Now, go, YOUR_CLASS. We will speak again, at a later date.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Taming the Beast

-- [DEPRECATED] Tears of the Poppy
    ["80258"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Tears of the Poppy",
    ["Description"]="Sinu a'manore, YOUR_CLASS.You have answered our call for aid, for which we are truly grateful.With the fall of Quel'Thalas we, the Quel'dorei, have been left without a home. It is here where we shall focus our wits and strengthen our will. This is the beginning of our quest for vengeance, and you shall be part of it, among others.You see, as we prepare for a war against death itself we need to have as less casualties as possible but we can only prevent so many.Where there is a battle there shall be dead and wounded. I ask of you on this day and many to come to aid us in our effort to supply our numbers with a means to mend and heal. There is a small and not so elegant flower growing in Redrige Mountains. We call it poppy. I shall not bore you with the alchemical details, you only need to know that the concoction will ease the pain of the wounded. I know it's a simple task  but it is not meaningless.Return to me when you have a handful of them.",
    ["Objectives"]="Gather ten poppies in Redridge Mountains.",
    ["Progress"]="This will make a difference in the battle to come, please do not take it lightly.",
    ["Completion"]="These will do just fine. Not all of them are of the highest quality but they will be useful. Thank you YOUR_CLASS.Ah yes, here is your reward.Return soon, YOUR_CLASS.Selama Ashal'anore!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Tears of the Poppy

-- [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search I
    ["80261"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search I",
    ["Description"]="Oh, great adventurer! My name is Teslinah. Please, I need your help!My mommy and I were in the Farstrider Lodge after fleeing from all the bad stuff up north, but when we were in Stormwind, we got separated! Miss Elsharin found me and took me here because she thought my mommy would be here, too, but she's not! The grumpy man over there only told me to sit in a corner and be silent. You'll help me, right?",
    ["Objectives"]="Search for Teslinah's mom in Stormwind.",
    ["Progress"]="Please, will you help me?Pretty please?",
    ["Completion"]="She's not in the Mage District. But we can't give up!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search I

-- [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search II
    ["80262"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search II",
    ["Description"]="Let's try the dwarven area, then the park, and then my peoples' district!",
    ["Objectives"]="Search for Teslinah's mom in Stormwind.",
    ["Progress"]="I'm going to cry really hard if we can't find her!",
    ["Completion"]="She's not here either... Mommy, where are you?!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search II

-- [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search III
    ["80263"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search III",
    ["Description"]="Let's try the big castle next! I hear the king's son is really nice. We can also try the old part of town. I think it has a tavern too. Oh, and let's look at that Gnomish tram I've heard about! Maybe she's waiting there.",
    ["Objectives"]="Search for Teslinah's mom in Stormwind.",
    ["Progress"]="We cannot give up! We have to find her. I don't know what I'd ever do without her.",
    ["Completion"]="Mommy is out there somewhere. Let's continue please!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search III

-- [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search IV
    ["80264"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search IV",
    ["Description"]="We could try the barracks in the Old Town. Oh, and that giant Cathedral place! Maybe she went to look for me there. I heard there's a place for lost children nearby in a pretty big building!",
    ["Objectives"]="Search for Teslinah's mom in Stormwind.",
    ["Progress"]="Please, keep helping me. She can't be far!",
    ["Completion"]="Mommy... N-No, I am sure we can find her, right?",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search IV

-- [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search V
    ["80265"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search V",
    ["Description"]="I don't think there's many other places left. Let's look everywhere we've missed. There's more to the Cathedral, and we can look in the Trade place!",
    ["Objectives"]="Find someone who can help find Teslinah's mom in Stormwind.",
    ["Progress"]="Yes? What can I do for you, YOUR_RACE?",
    ["Completion"]="Her mom is missing, you say? Give me a moment to look her up in our extensive collection of documents.The girl's name is Teslinah? We do have records of her and her mother's arrival in Stormwind with the other refugees, but the two of them never showed up at the City hall for their registration.This is a troubling discovery. We can't have people going missing in Stormwind. I will investigate, but until my investigation is completed, can I count on you to care for the girl?Since she was registered here in Stormwind, I will issue some bonds to feed her properly.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Teslinah's Search V

-- [DEPRECATED] Thalassian Accession
    ["40378"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Thalassian Accession",
    ["Description"]="There, it is done. I have prepared a writ for the High Priestess, explaining how instrumental you and the Quel'dorei were in slaying our ancient enemy Dra'lox Felstar.His deeds were unforgivable, which is why your actions may prove just enough to sway even the stern Archdruid Staghelm and his stringent followers.",
    ["Objectives"]="Present the Sealed Writ to Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus.",
    ["Progress"]="What news do you bring?",
    ["Completion"]="I know the message you bear. Word of Felstar's demise has been spreading swiftly.May the Night Warrior ever bear steel with you, YOUR_NAME. May such be the fate of all those who dare threaten us.<She lets out a long sigh.>You might have begun to glimpse the rift that divides Darnassus. Many of Fandral's druids have rescinded their former protests about the accession of the Quel'dorei, but the Archdruid himself remains unyielding.Yet with his support on the matter ebbing, nothing more ties my hands in granting Silvermoon my full support.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Thalassian Accession

-- [DEPRECATED] The Activation
    ["40132"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] The Activation",
    ["Description"]="Thank you again. I believe the core is installed. So now all that's left to do is the final assembly, and then we'll have this automaton working! Speak to me again and say the word. Then, we'll turn it on.",
    ["Objectives"]="Speak to Torble Sparksprocket and activate Analyzer X-51",
    ["Progress"]="Stand by... Processing.",
    ["Completion"]="Analyzer X-51 huh? The memory banks are restricted. I'll have to figure out how to unlock them. Imagine the secrets it may possess! The secrets of the Titans! He's very cooperative, though, so I'd say we've made some headway.I'll keep working with Analyzer X-51 and see if he can help the dig site for now. I'll call you once I have a hint regarding the memory banks. In the meantime, I have something for you. I have modified Analyzer X-51's old depleted power core into an amulet you can wear.While the energies within are but a fraction of what the core once held, it can still sustain your magical energies if you use magic... If not, I bet we can sell it to someone who'd be interested.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] The Activation

-- [DEPRECATED] The Kaldorei Problem
    ["40376"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] The Kaldorei Problem",
    ["Description"]="You have done well. I think it is high time for you to meet our leader. She awaits your arrival atop the Citadel.",
    ["Objectives"]="Ascend the summit of the Citadel of the Sun and speak to the leader of the Silvermoon Remnant.",
    ["Progress"]="So you are the one that everyone has been talking about. It's a pleasure to meet you, YOUR_NAME.My name is Vereesa Windrunner, and I wanted to personally thank you for your efforts in bringing our people closer to the Alliance.Although it is unfortunate that some Kaldorei still doubt our intentions, we will prove we are not what they would fear us to be.",
    ["Completion"]="You see, when the Scourge ravaged our lands, we were left beaten and broken. So I gathered those I could find and set out to reclaim this outpost. It was not an easy task, but now we have a place to call home.I only wish Prince Kael'thas could have seen all of this. But, now is not the time to mourn. We have to hold our heads high and look forward.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] The Kaldorei Problem

-- [Deprecated] The Lies that Bind Us
    ["80321"] = {
    ["Title"]="[Deprecated] The Lies that Bind Us",
    ["Description"]="You're the one that helped Miley find this, yeah?<Gazlowe holds up the belt you found in Dustwind Cave.>I've had a bit of diggin' done and I know who made it. Name's Kiro in Orgrimmar. Nice enough gal, even if she's a tad aggressive.I'm sure it's a long shot, but I need you to check with her and find out if she knows anything about this inscription. I've already had it deciphered, but Kiro might know more.",
    ["Objectives"]="Give Knobby's Belt to Kiro in the Valley of Honor.",
    ["Progress"]="What are you looking for?",
    ["Completion"]="Yes, YOUR_CLASS, I made this. What of it?",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [Deprecated] The Lies that Bind Us

-- [Deprecated] The Lies That Bind Us
    ["80322"] = {
    ["Title"]="[Deprecated] The Lies That Bind Us",
    ["Description"]="Hah! No leatherworker made these marks.This is fel magic. There's an outcast located in the Barrens. It's a blacksmith from our world. He has a gift when it comes to fel magic; he can sense the origin.You'll need payment if you seek him out, and you'll need luck on your side.Some of us don't like reliving our past. The taint that was in our blood haunts him still, as it does for many of us. Leave me be, now.Seek Vrang west of the road along the Barrens' northern foothills.",
    ["Objectives"]="Take Knobby's Belt and 20 silver to Vrang Wildgore in the Barrens.",
    ["Progress"]="A customer! Greetings, YOUR_CLASS. Take a look at what I have to offer.",
    ["Completion"]="Kiro sent you, no doubt. I didn't tell that cursed woman about my ability for her to send me customers!If she has an urgent enough reason, then just give me the coin and show me the mark of fel. But I don't promise you'll like the answer I have to give about its source.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [Deprecated] The Lies That Bind Us

-- [Deprecated] The Lies That Bind Us
    ["80323"] = {
    ["Title"]="[Deprecated] The Lies That Bind Us",
    ["Description"]="The magic that etched this belt came from Neeru Fireblade. I still cannot read the inscription, but with Neeru's hand in this, I can assure you that it is powerful. Go on your way now, YOUR_CLASS. I don't need the wrath of Neeru or his minions targeting me.",
    ["Objectives"]="Return to Gazlowe with Knobby's Belt.",
    ["Progress"]="Welcome back, YOUR_NAME. You still have the belt?",
    ["Completion"]="Interesting.<Gazlowe turns the belt over in his hands.>Neeru Fireblade, eh? I wonder what Neeru is trying to pull right under Thrall's nose?Go on, now, YOUR_NAME. I've got a few contacts to reach out to. I'll get in touch with you when the next step is to be taken.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [Deprecated] The Lies That Bind Us

-- [DEPRECATED] The Magical Ailment
    ["40380"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] The Magical Ailment",
    ["Description"]="With the Quel'dorei's accession to the Alliance, I do not doubt that it is only a matter of time before we rise to our former glory. But as my people celebrate, I must keep track of the problems that remain.For years my people relied on the magic of the great fount called the Sunwell. Its destruction made us realize how dependent we became on its energies.Without it, we are vulnerable to succumbing to magic addiction.Miraculously, the rangers who were hunting Dra'lox with you stumbled upon a mystical pool of restorative waters whose effects are reminiscent of the Sunwell.If this is true, it could be our salvation. I need you to travel to Darnassus and ask Ashylah Starcaller if such waters can be procured for the Quel'dorei.",
    ["Objectives"]="Travel to Darnassus and speak to Ashylah Starcaller.",
    ["Progress"]="I take it the Quel'dorei sent you. What can I do for you?",
    ["Completion"]="<Ashylah Starcaller blinks as you make your request.>You have to understand, YOUR_NAME, our moonwells are not like the Well of Eternity of old. Their waters have been cleansed, and sanctified by the Great Mother.They can replenish health, mana and even stave off hunger. But we hold them as hallowed shrines, we cannot grant them to others so easily.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] The Magical Ailment

-- [Deprecated] The Mail Must Go Through
    ["60121"] = {
    ["Title"]="[Deprecated] The Mail Must Go Through",
    ["Description"]="You know, since there's another shipment coming, I might as well just wait for them here. I got a few more coins here to spare, and so far my eye for talent hasn't lead me wrong with you.Now I know I want to hire more YOUR_CLASSs for later jobs, but we still have to get these weapon crates to Orgrimmar. A goblin's reputation is ninety percent of his business! How about it? Mind hauling this stuff the rest of the way for me?My no good cousin Kozish should have made it there hours ago. He had more cargo to deliver and is probably drinking away his paycheck at the first pub he saw by now. Check there for him in the Valley of Strength.",
    ["Objectives"]="Deliver Rezlak's Shipment to Rezlak's cousin Kozish in Orgrimmar.",
    ["Progress"]="I drink alone, pal.",
    ["Completion"]="<The goblin notices you over a giant gulp from his cup>.Yeah, what do you want? Oh the supplies made it? Too bad, I'm done with this gig.Maybe I could be a pirate...",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [Deprecated] The Mail Must Go Through

-- [Deprecated] The Oil Stops Flowing
    ["55001"] = {
    ["Title"]="[Deprecated] The Oil Stops Flowing",
    ["Description"]="Damned, blasted, stupid, good for NOTHING. Isn't this just great? It's one thing after another with that oil platform, and I'm a week behind schedule!If you don't call havin' two workers get sucked into the ocean and your oil platform over-run by lobsters a nightmare, then I don't know where you're from pal!The oil needs to keep flowing, and if the boss finds out that this has gone on, he'll have my head!Maybe I could blame this on someone, but first things first, get on over there and clear some of those blasted creatures so we can kick that baby into overdrive and start catching up on all the lost work!",
    ["Objectives"]="Kill 5 Makrura Oilclaws and 5 Makrura Threshers at the oil platform east of the Port.",
    ["Progress"]="You get rid of them yet? Time's tickin' here and I need that platform up and running!",
    ["Completion"]="Finally, I was devising a plan but all I could come up with was a flame thrower and a bomb. Big no-nos if ya know anything about oil safety!It might not be ALL of em, but a few less of the seafood is good enough for me!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [Deprecated] The Oil Stops Flowing

-- [DEPRECATED] The Pumpkin Thieves
    ["60041"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] The Pumpkin Thieves",
    ["Description"]="This is outrageous! The nerve! First, they sneak around and scare our livestock. Then, they sneak in and pillage our barn. What's next? Rob our house? Kill us all in our sleep?! What do you think the guards are doing about this situation, hm? NOTHING!These gnolls are getting bolder with every passing day, and I've had enough! The guards are of no help, but I see you've got some fire in your eye. Perhaps you can help keep me and my family safe?What? Pie? Listen here, those gnolls made off with all my pumpkins! Little barbarians have no idea how to cook anything besides crudely charring it! What in the blazes are they going to do with pumpkins?! If you want a pie so badly, go and get my pumpkins back.I've seen those mongrels scurry north across the road far beyond Goldshire. Perhaps someone at the Eastvale Logging Camp has seen where the little bandits are holed up. Ask the folks over there where my pumpkins have gone! While you're at it, put down as many of those filthy brigands as you can!",
    ["Objectives"]="Bring back 7 Elwynn Pumpkins to Gramma Stonefield.",
    ["Progress"]="Oh, tell me you put those dirty beasts in the ground! What about my pumpkins? Did you manage to find my sweet pumpkins?",
    ["Completion"]="By the Light!My dear child, I can't tell you what a blessing you've been to all of us here on the farm!You've done more than enough to earn a pie, YOUR_NAME! Take it with my deepest gratitude!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] The Pumpkin Thieves

-- [DEPRECATED] This Is In My Contract
    ["80121"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] This Is In My Contract",
    ["Description"]="Nert might be afraid of a little shadow magic, but you and I know what we're doing, yeah?It's time for you to learn how to summon your first demon! Yeah, I know we're in the middle of a crisis, but what better time to have a demon's aid?Besides, we're warlocks. Crises are what we're about! That and I'm contractually obligated to arm you to \"enforce\".While you're out on Nert's task, I want you to look for something that radiates darkness. That energy condenses into these purple crystals, see? Try to pinch one of those without getting yourself killed.Bring me back one of those crystals, and I'll teach ya how to summon an imp. Fair trade, yeah?",
    ["Objectives"]="Collect a Howling Crystal from one of the creatures of the Grumbling Grove.",
    ["Progress"]="Was I not crystal clear? I need a crystal full of shadow magic for the summoning spell.",
    ["Completion"]="Beautiful! This will do nicely.Now watch and learn, kid - You only get to forcibly rip a demon from the void for the first time once in your life.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] This Is In My Contract

-- [DEPRECATED] To Alah'Thalas!
    ["80251"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] To Alah'Thalas!",
    ["Description"]="Now that you know what we're dealing with and our history...The time has come to act. If you're truly interested in helping us, then this is the way.One of our most talented mages has established a leyline connection to Alah'thalas.Go to the Mage Tower in the Mage District, and speak to Elsharin. She will be able to take you there, once you arrive I am sure someone will tend to you.",
    ["Objectives"]="Speak to Elsharin, she can be found beyond the portal in the Mage Tower in Stormwind.",
    ["Progress"]="Oh my! What can I do for you, YOUR_RACE?",
    ["Completion"]="Oh you've come to assist Alah'thalas!I'm quite happy I must say, I knew Caledra could find nice people! I'm surprised she found a YOUR_CLASS as capable as you!The loss of Quel'thalas has grieved me greatly, but now I see hope, hope that our people can have a future again!Talk to me when you are ready and I will send you to Alah'thalas!",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] To Alah'Thalas!

-- [Deprecated] Triggered!
    ["60120"] = {
    ["Title"]="[Deprecated] Triggered!",
    ["Description"]="Now that introductions are out of the way, you and I are kinda like partners, yeah? Here's the thing, more than the general supplies sent from Ratchet we had a special order those harpies took. Those feathery fiends got their claws on at least two crates of weapons and ammo meant for Orgrimmar.Worse than the harpies is the tauren merchant expecting the goods. She might use me for target practice if she finds out her order got lost in delivery a second time.YOUR_NAME, I gotta get those crates back!",
    ["Objectives"]="Find Kaja's Ammunition from Ammo Crates in Razorwind Canyon and return to Rezlak near Orgrimmar.",
    ["Progress"]="I don't want to get shot. Do you?",
    ["Completion"]="Fantastic, you found them. I was getting worried thinking about harpies armed with rifles. You think they can pull a trigger with those talons? On second thought, never mind. I don't wanna think about it.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [Deprecated] Triggered!

-- [DEPRECATED] Vestia's Missive
    ["40383"] = {
    ["Title"]="[DEPRECATED] Vestia's Missive",
    ["Description"]="Take this. I have convinced a few of my fellow priestesses to vouch for you and your Quel'dorei friends, but know that creating a new moonwell for Alah'thalas to use will not be easy, even with our endorsement.Let us hope that the High Priestess will be amenable to extending her support once again.",
    ["Objectives"]="Deliver Vestia's Missive to Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus.",
    ["Progress"]="Yes?",
    ["Completion"]="Hail to you again, YOUR_NAME. What tidings do you bear?<Tyrande opens and reads the missive>I see. The ancestral sickness that once plagued even Dath'remar Sunstrider still assails the hearts of the Quel'dorei. That is a heavy burden to endure.",
    ["minlevel"]="0",
    ["questlevel"]="0",
    }, -- end [DEPRECATED] Vestia's Missive

